   "text": "This SMILES was written from the drawing as read, and I did not run it through a parser, so the valence and ring-closure checks are by eye. The stereocentres on the two prolines, the threonines, glutamate and biphenylalanines are partly guesses from hard-to-resolve wedges.\n\n**Left side (glycocluster):**\n- Three peracetylated \u03b2-D-GalNAc units, each linked through an O-(CH2)4-C(=O)-NH chain.\n- The bottom sugar carries an ethoxy group at C3 instead of an acetate, as drawn.\n- The top and bottom arms continue as NH-(CH2)3-NH-C(=O)CH2CH2-O-CH2- to a central quaternary carbon.\n- The middle arm is written as drawn: NH-CH2CH2-O-CH2-C(=O)-CH2CH2-O-CH2-.\n- The central carbon also carries NH-C(=O)-(CH2)6-C(=O)-NH, a suberoyl linker to the lysine side chain.\n\n**Peptide, read N to C:**\n1. The N-terminus is acylated by the CH2C(=O) of a thioether link to Cys.\n2. The residues run D-Phe, Val, D-Pro, Thr, Thr, Bip, N-Me-Ala, Bip, N-Me-Ala, Glu, Ala, Pro, Cys (Bip = biphenylalanine).\n3. The Cys side-chain sulfur closes the macrocycle through that CH2C(=O) group.\n4. After Cys the chain continues Gly, then Lys-NH2, where the lysine side-chain amine carries the suberoyl linker.\n\n**Stereochemistry:**\n- Assigned from the wedges: D-Phe, L-Val, L-Cys, L-Lys, L-Ala, L-N-Me-Ala, the top L-Pro, L-Bip.\n- Assumed or only tentatively read: L-Thr, L-Glu, and the bottom Pro as D.\n- Sugars are taken as \u03b2-D-galacto.\n\nSMILES: C(COCCC(=O)NCCCNC(=O)CCCCO[C@@H]1O[C@H](COC(C)=O)[C@H](OC(C)=O)[C@H](OC(C)=O)[C@H]1NC(C)=O)(COCCC(=O)COCCNC(=O)CCCCO[C@@H]1O[C@H](COC(C)=O)[C@H](OC(C)=O)[C@H](OC(C)=O)[C@H]1NC(C)=O)(COCCC(=O)NCCCNC(=O)CCCCO[C@@H]1O[C@H](COC(C)=O)[C@H](OC(C)=O)[C@H](OCC)[C@H]1NC(C)=O)NC(=O)CCCCCCC(=O)NCCCC[C@@H](C(N)=O)NC(=O)CNC(=O)[C@H](CS%11)NC(=O)[C@@H]1CCCN1C(=O)[C@H](C)NC(=O)[C@H](CCC(=O)O)NC(=O)[C@H](C)N(C)C(=O)[C@H](Cc2ccc(cc2)-c2ccccc2)NC(=O)[C@H](C)N(C)C(=O)[C@H](Cc2ccc(cc2)-c2ccccc2)NC(=O)[C@H]([C@@H](C)O)NC(=O)[C@H]([C@@H](C)O)NC(=O)[C@H]1CCCN1C(